WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.038
Avoid feature fever.

00:00:01.038 --> 00:00:03.461
Choose the next experiment that earns proof.

00:00:03.461 --> 00:00:06.921
This lesson is about what to build next (and not).

00:00:06.921 --> 00:00:09.343
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:09.343 --> 00:00:12.804
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:12.804 --> 00:00:17.995
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:17.995 --> 00:00:21.801
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:25.608
Stay practical: choose next experiment before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:25.928 --> 00:00:29.699
Choose one next experiment tied to sales or delivery pain.

00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:31.962
Remember the objective: choose next experiment.

00:00:31.962 --> 00:00:36.110
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:40.635
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:40.635 --> 00:00:44.783
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:49.308
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:49.308 --> 00:00:51.948
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:51.948 --> 00:00:53.456
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:53.776 --> 00:00:57.226
Not: redesign, new niche, or ten tools at once.

00:00:57.226 --> 00:00:59.526
Remember the objective: choose next experiment.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:03.743
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

